{
  "dom_id": "step-q164521",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "$$\nf(t,y)=\u27e8\\text{_____},\\,y,\\,2\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t\u27e9,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,y)$ above parametrizes one sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as ${z}^{2}-{x}^{2}=4$ for $z\\ge 2.$ What is the first component of $f?$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the hyperbola ${z}^{2}-{x}^{2}=4$ for $z\\ge 2$ in $xz$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n\u27e8x,z\u27e9=\u27e82\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t,\\,2\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t\u27e9,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =(2\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t)^{2}-(2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t)^{2} \\\\  & =4{sec}^{2}\u2061t-4{tan}^{2}\u2061t \\\\  & =4({sec}^{2}\u2061t-{tan}^{2}\u2061t) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,y) & =\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t,\\,y,\\,2\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t.$",
